IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tprai-types`

-- Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK) — GOAL 3:
-- INFORMATION AND DISCLOSURE (Schedule 1 paras 1-4).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2010-10.txt. The conversion drops
-- the paragraph numbers; they are, in order, paras 1-7.

§ `Goal 3 — information and disclosure`

DECLARE `Notice facts` HAS
    -- Para 1(1): A reasonably believes B has incurred a liability to A and B
    -- is a relevant person; the notice goes to B.
    `believes the recipient incurred a liability to them and is a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Para 1(2): A reasonably believes a liability was incurred to A, the
    -- person is insured against it, the rights were transferred to A, and
    -- the recipient C can provide the information.
    `believes an insured liability's rights were transferred to them and the recipient can inform` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing with the particulars relied on`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `received on`                                       IS A DATE

DECLARE `Disclosure notice facts` HAS
    -- Para 3(1): proceedings under the Act started against the insurer, the
    -- liability claimed against a body corporate or an unincorporated body
    -- other than a partnership, which has been dissolved.
    `proceedings started against a dissolved body's insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Para 3(2): the recipient was an officer or employee immediately before
    -- the transfer, or the insolvency practitioner or official receiver
    -- immediately before dissolution.
    `the recipient is within para 3(2)`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Para 3(3)
    `accompanied by the particulars of claim`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `received on`                                       IS A DATE

-- "The period of 28 days beginning with the day of receipt" ends on receipt +
-- 27.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last of the 28 days beginning with` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS 27)

-- Para 1(1)-(2), (6): a notice in writing, with the particulars of the facts
-- relied on, by a person with the reasonable belief in (1) or (2).
@ref Sch 1 para 1
GIVEN n IS A `Notice facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice requesting information may be given under` n IF
        (   n's `believes the recipient incurred a liability to them and is a relevant person`
         OR n's `believes an insured liability's rights were transferred to them and the recipient can inform`)
    AND n's `in writing with the particulars relied on`

-- Para 2(1) "A person (R) who receives a notice under paragraph 1 must,
-- within the period of 28 days beginning with the day of receipt of the
-- notice— (a) provide ... any information specified in it that R is able to
-- provide; (b) ... notify that person why R is not able to provide it."
@ref Sch 1 paras 1-2
@export The last day on which a person who received a valid notice under Schedule 1 para 1 to the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK) must provide the information (or say why it cannot), within the 28 days beginning with the day of receipt (receipt + 27); NOTHING if the notice was not one para 1 allows. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Notice facts`  @desc The beliefs behind the notice, whether it is in writing with particulars, and the day it was received
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to provide information under` n MEANS
    IF   `a notice requesting information may be given under` n
    THEN JUST (`the last of the 28 days beginning with` (n's `received on`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Para 3(1)-(3): a notice requiring disclosure, about a dissolved body.
-- Para 4(3) "A person who ... has to serve a list of documents must do so
-- within the period of 28 days beginning with the day of receipt of the
-- notice."
@ref Sch 1 paras 3-4
@export The last day on which a person who received a valid notice under Schedule 1 para 3 to the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK) must serve a list of documents (para 4(3)), within the 28 days beginning with the day of receipt (receipt + 27); NOTHING if the notice was not one para 3 allows. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Disclosure notice facts`  @desc Proceedings against a dissolved body's insurer, the recipient's role, the particulars of claim, and the day received
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to serve a list of documents under` n MEANS
    IF       n's `proceedings started against a dissolved body's insurer`
         AND n's `the recipient is within para 3(2)`
         AND n's `accompanied by the particulars of claim`
    THEN JUST (`the last of the 28 days beginning with` (n's `received on`))
    ELSE NOTHING
